20,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, moving desks is a mess! It takes forever to settle in, and the morning setup upstairs takes way too long.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The costs are rigid. We pay for the area regardless of headcount, and every single wire move costs us money.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It's unfair. Some people arrive much earlier than others, and the current plan leaves several people without any window light.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's worse than I thought. The noise varies wildly across the room, and our gear takes days of tweaking to be comfortable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Sitting together actually helps! The new joiners learned faster by overhearing us, and project handovers became way smoother.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if moving is expensive, maybe we should just pick one spot and stay there?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"That would save on the facilities quote, but we have to consider the long-term utility of the space.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, if proximity helps learning, we can't just let people sit anywhere randomly.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Rin, ""staying there"" sounds good, but not if I'm stuck in a noisy spot with a bad chair.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Yumi,,Exactly! We need a balance between learning from each other and not being annoyed by the noise.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we have to set up every morning, I'll lose all my break time!","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The billing is fixed, so we aren't saving money by shrinking the footprint, only by reducing changes.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we use a first-come system, the early birds always get the windows. That's not a fair way to work.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shion,,"If we shift around, I'll spend my whole life adjusting my monitor arm and footrest. It's inefficient.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I think we should prioritize the social and professional growth that comes from sitting near the right people.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just don't want a chaotic morning or a fortnight of boxes everywhere.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Stability seems to be the common thread for both the budget and the mental load.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. We need a system that is predictable and doesn't favor the early arrivals.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Shion,,Fixed positions are the only way to ensure the physical environment is actually tolerable.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"As long as those fixed positions are chosen to help us collaborate, I'm on board.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
48,3,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
49,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Free Address sounds like a nightmare for my schedule. Rotating Blocks is okay, but Fixed Desks by Function is the safest.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Free Address is too volatile. Rotating Blocks still incurs costs. Fixed Desks by Function is the most fiscally responsible.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Free Address is unfair due to arrival times. Rotating Blocks is a compromise, but Fixed Desks by Function allows for fair assignment.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shion,,Free Address and Rotating Blocks are out. I need my settings to stay put. Fixed Desks by Function is the only choice.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Free Address might kill the organic learning. Rotating Blocks is interesting, but Fixed Desks by Function lets us group by project.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, do you think Fixed Desks will stop us from talking to other groups?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Toshio,,We can still walk over to other desks; we just won't be paying to move the wires every month.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,It's the only way to ensure the window seats are distributed logically rather than by luck.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shion,,It's the only way to escape the printer noise permanently.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, I think as long as the ""functions"" are grouped smartly, we'll still interact plenty.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Rin,,"Okay, I'm convinced. Fixed Desks it is!","{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I agree. It minimizes the facilities spend and provides the most stability.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for Fixed Desks to ensure equity in the layout.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shion,,Fixed Desks. No other option is physically viable for me.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'll go with Fixed Desks too, provided we group the project strands together.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
